# A file's public top-level names and the parameters of its public fns
# make up its interface. They may be prelude names and need not be read,
# in the entry file as in an imported one (D86). Inside the file the
# name is the file's own.
max = 3
unread = 4
fn first(xs, len = 1) = xs[len - 1]
print(max, first([7, 8]), first([7, 8], len: 2))
# expect: 3 7 8
